    "default_visible": false,
    "default_opacity": 0.9,
    "legend_note": "The best guide to what a railway is actually for. Above 160 km/h is an intercity spine; 100–140 a regional line with a real service; under 100 usually a freight branch or a rural line running twice a day. Speed is the fastest recorded anywhere on that line code, so it describes the line, not the metre of track under you. Grey is no speed on record for 18% of lines — not a slow line."
